## 🧭 Learning Roadmap

---

### 🟢 Core Language Basics (C01 – C14)
> **Purpose:** Learn C++ syntax and execution flow

Covers:
- Syntax, comments, output
- Variables and data types
- Operators and precedence
- Strings and math
- Conditions and loops
- Arrays and multidimensional arrays

Focus:  
> Write correct C++ code and understand how it executes.

---

### 🟢 Functions and Abstraction (C15)
> **Purpose:** Organize reusable logic

Covers:
- Function basics and return values
- Parameters and default arguments
- Function overloading
- Inline functions and recursion
- Scope and lifetime
- Passing arrays to functions
- Pass by value vs pass by reference
- Returning references
- Function pointers
- Lambda functions

Focus:  
> Build reusable logic blocks and understand how data flows through functions.

---

### 🟢 Data Representation and Memory (C16 – C22)
> **Purpose:** Understand how C++ represents and manages data

Covers:
- Enumeration and structures
- References and const references
- Pointers and pointer arithmetic
- Dynamic memory allocation using new and delete
- Memory leaks and dangling pointers
- File operations using fstream
- Exception handling and custom exceptions

Focus:  
> Write safe, real-world C++ programs with proper memory handling.

---

### 🟢 Object-Oriented Programming (C++ Class)
> **Purpose:** Master professional C++ object-oriented design

Covers:
- Classes and objects
- Access specifiers and encapsulation
- Constructors and destructors
- Constructor overloading and initialization order
- Static members and static methods
- Friend functions and friend classes
- Inheritance:
  - Single inheritance
  - Multilevel inheritance
  - Multiple inheritance
- Constructor calling order in inheritance
- Method overriding and virtual functions
- Polymorphism
- Abstract classes and pure virtual functions
- Operator overloading
- Function templates and class templates

Focus:  
> Design maintainable, scalable, and encapsulated C++ systems.

---

## 📌 Philosophy

> *If fundamentals are weak, OOP feels confusing.*  
> *If fundamentals are strong, OOP feels natural.*

This repository focuses on:
- executable examples
- comments as the main teaching tool
- step by step learning progression
- professional C++ habits from day one

